# Map proof sheets are diagnostics: a couple of megabytes each, regenerated by
# `node tools/build-map.mjs` whenever you want one, and worth nothing in history.
# Committing them would put a new multi-megabyte blob in the repository every time
# somebody fixed one hex. Review a map change in docs/map/index.html, or generate
# the proof locally and look at that.
docs/map/*-proof.png

# Aim previews are the same kind of thing for a card: `node tools/aim-preview.mjs
# <code>` cuts a plate the way its card window and the explorer thumbnail will, so
# you can look at the crop before committing the three numbers that chose it. A few
# megabytes each, regenerated on demand, and worth nothing in history.
docs/art/aim/

# And `node tools/card-proof.mjs <code>` photographs the finished card so it can be
# put in front of somebody. The card is docs/cards/<code>.svg; this is a picture of
# it, and a picture of a generated file has no business in history either.
docs/art/proofs/

# And `node tools/ledger-proof.mjs` puts every seven-segment figure on one sheet
# at TRUE SIZE against a millimetre ruler, plus one enlarged so you can see what
# shape it is. It exists because the figures were drawn, validated, committed and
# looked at only enlarged - where they were perfect - and at 4.9 x 8.4 mm a row of
# them read as rosettes. A proof is a photograph of the artefact, never the
# artefact, and it does not belong in history either.
docs/ledger/proof/

node_modules/
.DS_Store
